<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Kelvin's update feed. Served at https://usekelvin.app/appcast.xml via a redirect to this
     file on main — so a release updates this by a commit, and the website is never touched.
     Each enclosure is signed with the Sparkle EdDSA key (docs/RELEASING.md); installed copies
     verify against the public key baked into their Info.plist.

     From the second release onwards each item also carries a <sparkle:deltas> block, so an update
     is a few MB rather than the whole 1.4 GB image again. Build it with scripts/make-delta.sh and
     paste what it prints: sparkle:deltaFrom is the OLD build's CFBundleVersion — the number in
     <sparkle:version>, not the marketing version — because that is the key Sparkle looks a delta
     up by on the machine being updated. -->
